## Skills that auto-apply (no /command needed)

- `diagnosing-bugs` — when user reports a bug
- `tdd` — when user wants test-first
- `domain-modeling` — when user asks about CONTEXT.md or terms
- `grilling` — when user wants to stress-test a plan
- `codebase-design` — when user asks about module design
- pstack `how` — before editing existing code
- pstack `unslop` — on all agent-written prose
- `context7-mcp` — when any library is mentioned

## Skills requiring /command

- `/grilling` (explicit plan review)
- `/triage` (GitHub issue workflow)
- `/to-issues` (split into issues)
- `/ask-matt` (routing help)

## Pharmacy safety (hard boundary)

Never write code or give advice that:
- Diagnoses an illness or symptom
- Recommends a medication dose
- Replaces a pharmacist or prescription
- Makes an autonomous triage decision
- Sends LLM output directly to patients (shadow mode only until P2 owner review)

See `docs/SAFETY_RULES.md`.

## Skills to skip for BaleMed

Do not load these — they conflict or add no value:

- Cloudflare, Netlify, Sentry, magic-patterns, Coralogix, Zapier
- pstack: `arena`, `automate-me`, `interrogate`, `recall`, `reflect`, `teach`, all `principle-*`
- Browser automation, Browserbase Functions
- `continual-learning`

